  "steps": [
    {
      "t": "Mix sauce (minus peanut butter)",
      "x": "Combine soy, fish sauce, lime juice, sugar, sesame oil, Sriracha, garlic, ginger, coconut milk and water. Keep peanut butter aside.",
      "min": null
    },
    {
      "t": "Pressure cook",
      "x": "Chicken into the pot, pour sauce over, stir to coat. Seal, Pressure Cook High 8 min. Natural release 5 min, then quick release.",
      "min": 8
    },
    {
      "t": "Add peanut butter",
      "x": "Open lid, add peanut butter, stir vigorously until dissolved. Taste: more lime for brightness, soy for salt, Sriracha for heat.",
      "min": null
    },
    {
      "t": "Reduce if needed",
      "x": "Too thin? Sauté mode, simmer 3–4 min, stirring, until it coats the chicken.",
      "min": 4
    },
    {
      "t": "Serve",
      "x": "Over rice with spring onion, crushed peanuts and a lime wedge.",
      "min": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Peanut butter goes in after pressure cooking; it scorches and turns grainy under pressure.",
    "Leg meat only; breast dries out.",
    "Meal prep: store chicken and rice separately. Fridge 3 days."
